# Served by Workers static assets without invoking the Worker (see
# run_worker_first in wrangler.toml). Cross-origin isolation is what gives the
# low-latency engine SharedArrayBuffer.
#
# The CSP: our own scripts and nothing else, no frames either way (nothing
# can put the site in a frame to click it for you, and no frame inside it),
# and connections to the site and, for the app's --browser mode, its bridge
# on this machine. Styles may be inline (the overlay's page has one; Vue sets
# some), images may be data: (avatars). 'wasm-unsafe-eval' is for live
# captions' recognisers, which are WebAssembly (Vosk's, and ONNX Runtime's
# for Parakeet): it lets our own scripts compile WebAssembly, and nothing
# else (no eval, no new Function: scripts/vosk-glue.ts takes those out of
# Vosk's glue). Their workers are our own files, so worker-src stays 'self'.
/*
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'wasm-unsafe-eval'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: blob:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' ws://127.0.0.1:*; worker-src 'self'; media-src 'self' blob:; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'self'; frame-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  Permissions-Policy: microphone=(self), camera=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=()
